/*
:name: loop_array_port_ssa_rebuild
:type: equiv
:verilog_top: loop_array_port_ssa_rebuild.top
:pyrope_top: top
*/
// A rolled loop reading an ARRAY input port, in a unit whose accumulator is
// re-initialized before the loop (`total = 0` after `mut total:U12 = 0`).
// The repeated definition forces upass.ssa's full SSA rebuild, which re-emits
// every io port as a flat prim_type_int (the array view survives only in
// io_meta). The loop planner typed the lifted invariant `b` from that flat
// io slot, so `top.__loop0` got a plain 32-bit `b` and lnast.tolg failed
// "field/index read of 'b' could not be resolved". Dropping the re-init
// compiled. (lhdtrack item 2: the Pyrope writer re-emitted exactly this.)
pub mod top(b:[4]U8) -> (z:U12@[0]) {
  mut total:U12 = 0
  total = 0
  for i in 0..=3 {
    total = total + b[i]
  }
  z = total
}
